{"text": "09/25/95\n\n07:55 202 637 1505 PHILIP MORRIS CO\n\nPoints you can make in your Letter\n\nFollowing are some points you may want to make in your\n\n1 Senet\n\nletter to Feel free to use these points,\n\nor to put them in your own words. Your letter doesn't have\nto be long, it just needs to get the point across, that FDA\n\nregulation of cigarettes is unacceptable.\n\n\u2018Everyone agrees that minors should not smoke. But the\nFDA's plan to address the problem does very little to get at\nthe source of youth smoking -- access to cigarettes.\nInstead, the FDA plan would infringe on the ability of adult\n\nsmokers to purchase and enjoy cigarettes.\n\n\u201cCertainly the FDA and the White House have more important\n\nthings to do than dictate politically-correet behavior.\n\n\u2018Banning tobacco company sponsorship of musical, cultural\nand sporting events would devastate many of those events.\n\nResults might include higher ticket prices and fewer events.\n\n\u2018Promotional items encourage brand loyalty \u00bby rewarding\nadult smokers. The items have never been shown to cause\n\npeople to begin smoking.\n\n\u2018The president has given the FDA permission to regulate\ntobacco at a time when the agency is woefully unable to\n\nfulfill gts current obligations, including the approval of\n\n@oosoie\n\nO9IPCSTHEOS",
